{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"b7babf03490a8065","type":"text","text":"## <center>**RESEARCH QUESTION**</center>","x":-540,"y":-280,"width":506,"height":68},
		{"id":"2a37387d1e6ad336","type":"text","text":"<center>How can planetary health education be designed, implemented and evaluated within GP training in Flanders to equip GPs with the knowledge and competencies needed to address and mitigate climate- and environment-related health risks and to provide environmentally responsive, sustainable and equitable primary care?\n</center>","x":-540,"y":-167,"width":506,"height":1106},
		{"id":"77bd5d019eef535f","type":"text","text":"## <center>**SUB-QUESTIONS**</center>","x":35,"y":-280,"width":506,"height":68},
		{"id":"8c653ee81d11e62a","type":"text","text":"<center>In which extent and manner are sustainable care, health and environment, and GECs currently integrated in medical and GP training programmes in Belgium and Europe?</center>","x":35,"y":-167,"width":506,"height":225},
		{"id":"0181fac39d588e68","type":"text","text":"## <center>**METHODOLOGY**</center>","x":627,"y":-280,"width":857,"height":68},
		{"id":"80b740245e55c4ce","type":"text","text":"<center>Scoping review (building upon S. De Laere until 2022)</center>","x":627,"y":-167,"width":857,"height":113},
		{"id":"7ad327207650b333","type":"text","text":"<center> What are the current competency gaps and educational needs among GP trainees, supervisors and other relevant stakeholders in Flanders?</center>","x":35,"y":129,"width":506,"height":225},
		{"id":"2cf06956c23cbcd1","type":"text","text":"<center>Mixed-Methods</center>","x":627,"y":129,"width":174,"height":225},
		{"id":"30fb1b582262cd4e","type":"text","text":"<center>Cross-sectional surveys (knowledge/attitudes/perceptions)</center>","x":1122,"y":129,"width":362,"height":74},
